    "description": "Developed a MySQL statistical analysis database application in Java as part of a 44 million dollar program for the U.S. Air Force as a subcontractor\n•\tWorked on the proposal, basis of estimate, schedules, requirements, design, implementation and test\n•\tAlways met customer’s expectations and in several occasion was recognized for quality and drive \n•\tPresented in several Technical Inter-exchange Meetings (TIM) where customers indicated their satisfaction with the quality of the presentation\n\nDeveloped an automation tool to analyze the Cellworx network (ATM over SONET/SDH) for the U.S. Air Force and a Business Campus in Raleigh-Durham \n•\tDebugged and repaired software and hardware issues in the network - Management communication, fault management, performance monitoring, Quality of Service (QOS), policing, multicast, protection, and network virtualization (ex. VLAN)\n•\tThe network analyzer tool was used before executing critical missions and was developed using C/C++,  SNMP, Expect, and Linux scripts\n•\tThe network analyzer tool was ported to a DISA STIGs harden Redhat Live CD  \n•\tUpdated the network to meet  newer Cybersecurity guidelines within cost\n•\tDeveloped new procedures which improved operational efficiency and incident response time\n•\tAwarded preferred vendor status after several outstanding evaluations \n\nDeveloped engineering solutions for a real-time embedded controller using the PIC microcontrollers assembly \n•\tServices included requirements, designs, implementation, integration, verification, and validation \n•\tBuilt a strong working relationship with customer and vendor which lead to new business\n",
