    "description": "Cybersecurity: \n•\tLead an interdepartmental effort to standardize ESA’s corporate product security policies, processes, and procedures in accordance with the National Instituted Standards and Technology (NIST) Risk Management Framework (RMF) - Publications use;  FIPS 199, FIPS 200, FIPS 140-2, NIST SP 800.30, NIST SP 800.37, NIST SP 800.39, NIST SP 800.53/A, NIST SP 800.128, NSTISSSAM1-92 and NSTISSAM2-95\n•\tKnowledgeable in system engineering methodologies, system hardening, security engineering principles, Common Weakness Enumeration CWE, basic Red / Black separation (TEMPEST), and protection of data at rest (Anti-Tamper)\n•\tCybersecurity Activities included developing an Authorization Package, Security Controls and requirements, Security and Technical Planning, threat and vulnerability assessments, system hardening in accordance with the DISA/NSA STIGs, and Security Testing and Evaluation \n\nSystem:\n•\tResponsiblities included Proposal, Requirements, Architecture, Design, Implementation, Integration, Verification, and Validation phases using Agile development process\n•\tLead the Test team which included planning informal and formal testing (Qualification testing), Requirement Verification Matrix (RVM / VCRM) (test to requirement traceability), Test Readiness Review (TRR) and Final Configuration Acceptance (FCA)\n\nSoftware:\n•\tLead several multiprocessor efforts on AH-64 Apache Helicopter Mission Computer, V-22 Osprey Mission Computer, Bradley Smart Display, and Digital Map \n•\tThe Software development ranged from PIC microcontroller, boot code, interrupt handlers, memory management, UARTs, timebase timer, low-level drivers, Built-In Test (BIT), Board Support Package (BSP), multitasking, Real Time embedded Operating Systems (RTOS) (Wind River and Green Hills), Monolithic OS (Windows and Red Hat Linux), and embedded applications for Operational Flight Programs (OFP) \n•\tOther responsibilities was setting up the test environments and the development environments\n\n",
